<title>FAROE ISLANDS: SOCCER-FAROE ISLANDS BEAT MALTA 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-FAROE ISLANDS BEAT MALTA 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>TOFTIR, Faroe Islands 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Faroe Islands</p>
<p>beat Malta 2-1 (halftime 2-0) in their World Cup European group</p>
<p>six qualifier on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Faroe Islands - Uni Arge 6. Todi Jonsson 41</p>
<p>Malta - Gilbert Agius 47 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,400</p>
<p>Red cards: Jan Dam (FI) 47, Lawrence Attard (M) 83</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Faroe Islands: 1-Jens Martin Knudsen, 2-Oli Johannesen,</p>
<p>3-Jens Kristian Hansen, 4-Pol Thorsteinsson, 5-Oessur Hansen,</p>
<p>6-Allan Moerkoere, 7-Henning Jarnskoer, 8-Jan Dam, 9-Julian</p>
<p>Johnsson, 10-Todi Jonsson, 11-Uni Arge</p>
<p>Malta: 1-Mario Muscat, 2-Jeffrey Chetcuti, 3-Noel Turner,</p>
<p>4-Silvio Vella, 5-Darren Debono (14-Lawrence Attard, 33), 6-Ivan</p>
<p>Zammit, 7-Gilbert Agius, 8-Nicholas Saliba, 9-David Carabott,</p>
<p>10-Joseph Brincat, 11-Stefan Sultana</p>
</text>
